## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a pluggable, runtime-extensible routing system without touching the dispatcher. Emphasizes trade-offs between reflection vs factory-based resolution and thread-safe registries.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern for per-type behavior
- Registry/Factory for runtime extensibility
- Thread-safety, lazy initialization, and lifecycle of handlers

## Code Example
```javascript
class EventHandler {
  constructor() {}
  handle(event) { /* implement in subclass */ }
  type() { return this.constructor.name; }
}
class HandlerRegistry {
  constructor() { this.map = new Map(); }
  register(type, ctor) { this.map.set(type, ctor); }
  resolve(type) { const ctor = this.map.get(type); return ctor ? new ctor() : null; }
  dispatch(event) { const h = this.resolve(event.type); h && h.handle(event); }
}
```

